@* Single source of truth for the page-builder guide content — reused by both
   PageEditor.razor's "Rehber" modal and the full-page /admin/guide view, so the
   two never drift out of sync.

   Each section is a <details> so the guide reads as a list of questions rather
   than one long wall of text. Native <details> was chosen over a Blazor toggle on
   purpose: it costs no component state, works identically inside the modal and the
   page, and — crucially — the deep links below still work, because the anchor ids
   sit on the <details> elements and a browser opens a collapsed <details> when it
   scrolls to a target inside it. *@

<div class="guide-sections">
    @* First, because it answers the question every other section assumes:
       where things are. Written after the editor was reorganised into two side
       columns and one page-settings panel. *@
